1. Direct Contact Transmission:
Direct contact transmission occurs when a pathogen is transferred from one person to another through physical contact. This can happen through skin-to-skin contact, such as touching or kissing, or through contact with contaminated surfaces, such as touching a doorknob or eating contaminated food.
2. Indirect Contact Transmission:
Indirect contact transmission occurs when a pathogen is transferred from one person to another through contaminated objects or surfaces. This can happen through contact with contaminated food, water, or other objects, such as toys or utensils.
