Two-factor authentication (2FA) adds an extra layer of security to your online accounts by requiring a second form of verification in addition to your password. This could be a code sent to your phone or email, or a fingerprint scan. Enabling 2FA can significantly reduce the risk of unauthorized access to your accounts.

